fudd -- talk like Elmer Fudd============================    fuddA stdin-to-stdout filter that rewrites text the way Elmer Fudd would sayit: r and l both become w, th becomes d, so every sentence comes out inhis hunting lisp.  Pipe any text through it:    echo "Be very quiet, I am hunting rabbits." | fudd    fudd < READMEFrom the `silly' collection of dialect filters posted to Usenet; a lexprogram, its scanner generated here with the disk's own flex from fudd.l(in SRC/fudd/ORIG).